    { math: '1 · Gauss (electric): charge makes field', note: 'Electric field lines begin and end on charges. The field poking out of any closed box counts the charge inside. Positive sources, negative sinks.' },
    { math: '2 · Gauss (magnetic): no magnetic charge', note: 'Field lines through any closed box net to zero — magnetic field lines always close on themselves. There are no isolated north poles.' },
